.TH "LIBXWIIMOTE" 7 "August 2026" "WiiLand" "WiiLand Manual"
.SH NAME
libxwiimote \- display-server-independent Wii Remote access library
.
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B #include <xwiimote.h>
.
.SH DESCRIPTION
The libxwiimote compatibility library is implemented by the Rust
.B xwiimote
crate.  It discovers hid-wiimote devices through udev and exposes their kernel
input interfaces through the existing
.B xwii_*
API.  It does not require, connect to, or route events through Wayland, X.org,
XWayland, or any other display server.
.PP
The
.B wiilandd
daemon uses this library for ingestion and translates events into Linux uinput
virtual evdev devices.  Applications may also use the library directly when
they need finer-grained access than a display or kernel input path provides.
The resulting event data is therefore suitable for either Wayland or X.org
sessions and for non-display consumers.
.
.SH ABI COMPATIBILITY
The public declarations are in
.B lib/xwiimote.h
and all 26 exported symbols and version nodes are in
.B libxwiimote.sym .
The shared library retains SONAME
.B libxwiimote.so.2
and the static archive is
.B libxwiimote.a .
The Rust implementation preserves the existing event layouts and
discriminants, negative-errno/NULL/-1 error conventions, C allocator ownership,
stable file-descriptor readiness, monitor enumeration boundary and
deduplication, partial dispatch-size copies, and SYN_DROPPED recovery.  Opaque
handles validate null pointers and no panic crosses the C ABI.
.
.SH PERMISSIONS
The process using libxwiimote needs permission to read the hid-wiimote
.B /dev/input/event*
nodes for read-only interfaces.  Opening an interface with
.B XWII_IFACE_WRITABLE
requests read/write access and may additionally require write permission; the
library does not elevate privileges.  LED and other sysfs attributes have
their own permissions.
.PP
The packaged
.B res/70-wiiland-uinput.rules
rule tags hid-wiimote event nodes for active-seat access and supplies an
.B input
group,
.B 0660
fallback.  The packaged
.B res/70-udev-wiiland.rules
rule grants the input group write access to wiimote LED brightness attributes
for tools that use them.  Install the rules through the distribution's normal
udev configuration; active-seat ACL and group policy determine effective
permissions.
.
.SH BUILD AND INSTALLATION
The library is part of the Rust 1.98.0 Cargo workspace.  Build it with:
.PP
.RS
.B "cargo xtask build --release"
.RE
.PP
The xtask build compiles the Rust
.B rlib
and
.B staticlib ,
then final-links the versioned shared object from
.B libxwiimote.a
with the ABI map in
.B libxwiimote.sym
and SONAME
.B libxwiimote.so.2 .
The typed installation workflow installs the shared and static libraries,
header, pkg-config metadata, and applicable documentation:
.PP
.RS
.B "cargo xtask install --release --prefix /usr --sysconfdir /etc"
.br
.B "cargo xtask install --release --destdir PATH --prefix /usr \e"
.br
.B "  --sysconfdir /etc"
.RE
.PP
Pass
.B --with-udev-rules-dir auto|no|PATH
to select the udev integration destination.  DESTDIR stages files without
changing paths embedded in generated metadata.
.
.SH ARCHIVAL REFERENCES
Protocol history and device captures are retained in
.B doc/PROTOCOL ,
.B doc/DEVICES ,
.B doc/DEV_REMOTE ,
.B doc/eeprom.dump ,
and
.B doc/rdesc.dump .
They describe the hardware and wire-level lineage; the public header and symbol
map remain authoritative for the current C ABI.
.
